.TH CSTRING_COPY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_copy \- create an independent copy of a string
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cstring.h>

cstr cstring_copy(cstr s, char **err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Allocates a new cstring with the same content as s. The two strings are
fully independent after the call.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s     String to copy
err   Optional pointer to receive an error string on failure
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
New cstring on success
NULL on allocation failure (details written to *err if err is non-NULL)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Caller must destroy the returned cstring when done
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_substring (3),
.BR cstring_create (3)
